# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  TOUCH — Frontend environment
#
#  Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle at build time.
#  Anything here is PUBLIC and readable by anyone who views the site.
#  Never put a secret, API secret, or database credential in this file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the API.
#
#   Leave EMPTY when the frontend and API are served from the same origin
#   (e.g. behind one reverse proxy, or using the dev proxy in vite.config.js).
#   The client then calls the relative path `/api`, which keeps the refresh
#   cookie same-site and avoids CORS entirely — the simplest setup.
#
#   Set it to the full API origin only when they are on different domains,
#   e.g. https://api.yourstore.com/api
#   In that case the backend must also set COOKIE_SAMESITE=none and list this
#   site in CORS_ORIGINS.
VITE_API_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Storefront copies of commerce settings
#
#  The API is always the authority — pricingService decides what a customer is
#  actually charged. These exist only so that copy rendered BEFORE a cart exists
#  (the announcement strip, the product-page service facts, the policy pages)
#  quotes the same numbers.
#
#  If you change FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD, SHIPPING_FLAT_RATE or
#  ORDER_CANCEL_WINDOW_HOURS on the backend, change the matching value here and
#  rebuild the frontend, or the site will advertise one number and charge
#  another. Leave them unset to use the defaults, which match the backend
#  defaults.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD=1499
# VITE_SHIPPING_FLAT_RATE=79
# VITE_RETURN_WINDOW_DAYS=7
# VITE_ORDER_CANCEL_WINDOW_HOURS=24
